    "museum_caption_sub": "30 bronze gears calibrated to predict eclipses and Olympic cycles. Found 42 meters deep off the island of Antikythera (Greece).",
    "act1_kicker": "I · THE ORIGIN IN THE AEGEAN SEA (35°52′N, 23°18′E)",
    "act1_title": "The first computer in history was born in Europe. Your future must too.",
    "act1_p1": "In the spring of 1901, sponge divers rescued from the bottom of the Aegean Sea, off the small Greek island of Antikythera, a block of corroded bronze that forever changed the history of science. That artifact—designed in the astronomical and mechanical tradition of Archimedes of Syracuse—contained a system of gears capable of calculating with mathematical precision the movement of the cosmos sixteen centuries before any European clock.",
    "act1_p2": "Two millennia later, we are experiencing a geopolitical anomaly: by chance in the postal geography of the 1990s, the domain that identifies Artificial Intelligence throughout the planet (.ai) belongs to a Caribbean island foreign to our democratic governance. Europe has enacted the most guaranteeing laws in the world, but continues to rent the digital land where the future lives.",
    "act2_kicker": "II · THE EUROPEAN TRIANGLE OF TRUST",
    "act2_title": "What changes for you when the .IA domain exists",
    "act2_lead": "A citizen does not sign for a technical acronym in an ISO or ICANN table; signature to know who you can trust when interacting with a machine. Final Decision C(2026) 7098 validates the three mandates of our initiative:",
    "pillar1_tag": "OBJECTIVE 1 · ART. 172 AND 173 TFEU",
    "pillar1_title": "High Trust Digital Districts",
    "pillar1_body": "Creation of a community framework of test environments (regulatory sandboxes) and trans-European infrastructures for researchers, startups and universities to develop ethical AI on European soil without bureaucratic suffocation.",
    "pillar2_tag": "OBJECTIVE 2 · REGULATION (EU) 2019/517",
    "pillar2_title": ".IA Namespace Sovereignty",
    "pillar2_body": "Mandate for the European Commission to exercise its external representation powers before ISO (Agency 3166) and ICANN/IANA in order to protect, reserve and assign the .IA domain as a strategic European asset, following the legal precedent of the .eu domain.",
    "pillar3_tag": "OBJECTIVE 3 · ART. 16 AND 114 TFEU",
    "pillar3_title": "The Single Passport: eIDAS 2.0 + AI Act + GDPR",
    "pillar3_body": "That the technical resolution of a .ia domain itself guarantees by design three certainties to the citizen: verified identity (eIDAS 2.0), transparent algorithmic audit (AI Act) and absolute protection of personal data (GDPR).",
    "ship_caption": "The shipwreck of Antikythera (c. 87 BC): where ancient knowledge waited two thousand years to re-enlighten Europe.",
